.Dd $Mdocdate: October 20 2026$
.Dt WBANISH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wbanish
.Nd hide the Wayland mouse cursor when a key is pressed
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl i Ar modifier
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
hides the mouse cursor when a key is pressed.
The cursor is shown again when the mouse is moved, a button is pressed or
the wheel is scrolled.
Pressing a modifier key on its own does not hide the cursor.
.Pp
On GNOME,
.Nm
hides the cursor through its GNOME Shell extension,
.Ic wbanish@ksobitov.github.io ,
which it enables by itself and which also notices the key presses.
Elsewhere the compositor must support the wlr-layer-shell protocol, and
the user must be able to read the keyboards in
.Pa /dev/input ,
usually by being in the
.Ic input
group.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Print debugging messages to stderr.
.It Fl i Ar modifier
Ignore pressed key if
.Ar modifier
is used.
Modifiers are:
.Ic shift ,
.Ic control
or
.Ic ctrl ,
.Ic alt
or
.Ic mod1 ,
.Ic super
or
.Ic mod4 ,
.Ic altgr
or
.Ic mod5 ,
.Ic capslock
or
.Ic lock ,
.Ic numlock
or
.Ic mod2 ,
and
.Ic all ,
which means every held modifier but not CapsLock or NumLock.
May be given more than once.
.It Fl t Ar seconds
Hide the mouse cursor after
.Ar seconds
have passed without mouse activity.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv SIGUSR1
Pause, or resume if paused.
While paused the cursor is never hidden.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xbanish 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Outside GNOME,
.Nm
hides the cursor by covering every output with a transparent surface.
A click or scroll that brings the cursor back is therefore not passed on to
the window underneath.
